{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/253242-weapons-of-fate","id":253242,"title":"Weapons of Fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-09T05:14:00-07:00","id":253242,"title":"Weapons of Fate","content":"During the recent discussion f &quot;Scion fans! All of you-&quot; I posted an 'example topic' that read:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Mj\u00f6lnir is but the first of a new kind of weapon that the gods have developed and are testing via the newer pantheon&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>...and that made me think of actual super weapons of the Overworld. I mean, much like we humans have powerful weapons, so does the gods... and this is the place to tell others about them! So please share any of the relics and artifacts that have popped up in your games that altered the world! Things like Mj\u00f6lnir and Zeus thunderbolt!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Genesis Ring (Fate Relic \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <img src=\"http://fc07.deviantart.net/fs71/i/2010/327/f/5/nevinyrral__s_disk_by_steveargyle-d33gixs.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <b>The Myth:</b> Who built the ring is unknown. It's said that Loki found it during his travels in Africa together with Set as they sought a way to free themselves of their respective burdens of fate. He hid it from Set by keeping it in his mouth as they traveled north. Set of course, suspected something and commanded Loki to speak by using his true name. Loki spoke and revealed nothing of the Genesis Ring as he had already spirited it away via illusions. None the wiser, Set returned home and Loki had time to inspect his relic.<br /> <br /> The relic however, activated and nearly destroyed Loki with its power. Surely he would've ended if his fate had not already been put in Ragnarrok. The ring flung away and was burried deep into the antarctic snow. Now, Loki wishes to find the ring, but dares not approach it a second time, unless his fate be rewritten into that of nothingness...<br /> <br /> <b>The Truth:</b> The Ring was found by Loki and its one of the last vestiges of Ra's ancient omnipotence. The ring was created by him as an experiment and when Isis tricked him into revealing his true name, he forgot about the ring. If Ra were to find out that some measure of his omnipotence still remained in the world, he would pay dearly to have it handed back to him.<br /> <br /> <b>The Twist: </b>Set has always known about the ring. He has been searching for it for ages and it was pure chance (or fate) that Loki found it first. Set would do anything, including walking over the bodies of other gods, to get a grip on the item. He hopes to use the item to rule a new world instead of this one.<br /> <br /> <b>The Powers:</b> The purpose of the ring is to create a new world. Once outside the borders of any well defined overrealm, the ring can be spoken to by the use of its own true name. The process to figure this out most contest against a Legend 13 beeing (the effective legend of ra before he lost his omnipotence). If one figures it out however, one can define who gets to enter the new world or not. This new &quot;World&quot; will be a wild place without humans. Thus the god who activates this ring, might be the only god to ever appear in that world... Anyone in close proximity will recieve 10 aggravated damage each 5 ticks inside the area, which is as far as the ring can be seen.<br /> <br /> Holding the ring lets the wielder add his legend as successes to any Craft, Occult or Science roll for 1 legend point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","user":"Gemstone","date":". 09-10-2014, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:16:34-07:00","id":258209,"title":"","content":"I think the Hindu have had the lock on supernatural weaponry for centuries, if not millennia. I look to them for inspiration for such things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astra_(weapon)\" target=\"_blank\">Astra weapons</a> The big gun (literally a nuke) was from the Creator himself, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brahmashira\" target=\"_blank\">Brahmashira</a><br /> <br /> <i>The Brahmashira was never used in war, as it had four times more power than the Brahmastra, i.e. Fourth power square, as the name suggests, since Brahma has Four Heads.<br /> The weapon was also believed to cause severe environmental damage. The land where the weapon was used became barren and all life in and around that area ceased to exist, as both men and women became infertile. There was also a severe decrease in rainfall with the land developing cracks, like in a drought. The Brahmastra is mentioned in the epics and vedas as a weapon of last resort and was never to be used in combat. There are various descriptions of weapons created by Hindu deities such as, Brahmastra, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaumodaki\" target=\"_blank\">Kaumodaki</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narayanastra\" target=\"_blank\">Narayanastra</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaishnavastra\" target=\"_blank\">Vaishnavastra</a>, Bhargavastra, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pashupatastra\" target=\"_blank\">Pashupatastra</a>,<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiva_Dhanush\" target=\"_blank\">Shiva Dhanush</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudarshana_Chakra\" target=\"_blank\">Sudarshana Chakra</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trishul_(weapon)\" target=\"_blank\">Trishul</a>, and the personal weapons of the gods, the trishul, chakram and the brahmadanda, are the most powerful weapons.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}